{
  "slug": "habit",
  "name": "Habit",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Intelligent, quick, and lightweight prompt inventory. Observes, captures, and evolves reusable prompts and workflows into a living, browsable collection.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `distill` (Use when the user wants to extract reusable patterns from their session, restructure the habit inventory, or scan…), `edit` (Use when the user wants to create a new habit or update an existing one through natural language), `habit` (Use when the user mentions habits, saved prompts, reusable workflows, repeated commands, or their prompt inventory), `run` (Use when the user wants to execute a saved habit directly by name, with optional overrides), `suggest` (Use when the user wants to apply relevant habits to their request without naming them individually), `watch` (Use when the user wants to check, pause, or resume automatic habit capture)\n- **Hooks** (3): `UserPromptSubmit`, `SessionStart`, `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install habit@claude-community` from `Prog-Jacob/habit`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "hook": 3
  },
